WEBVTT

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.290
You're not going to attempt a rescue mission?

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.560
You must be joking or something...

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.390
We're talking about nobles being assaulted now.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.420
Around two hours ago,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:02.340
at a train station near the border, we arrested a man trying to bring the documents to foreign media outlets.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.810
We found out about tonight's assault from him.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.840
It was too late.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.270
Just too late.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:18.780
I'm guessing that at least ten people are dead at the scene already.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.290
I see...

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.850
"We weren't able to prevent casualties even after gaining this intelligence."

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.120
This kind of "stain" has no place in the glorious Section I.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.800
That's your logic, right?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.720
The blockade around the ballroom hall area you established...

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:43.610
...is just for "coincidentally" arresting the suspicious civilian mob that's headed for the ballroom hall, eh?

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:51.980
And that's when we officially knew about the tragedy and asserted...

00:02:53.880 --> 00:03:01.240
...that if we had more power and authority, we could have prevented this tragedy.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.490
But...

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:17.250
...there might be a small chance there are no casualties, yet.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.620
The night's still young, too.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.770
See 'ya later.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:44.540
For a situation as serious as this to not result in any casualties yet...

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:48.760
...rather than calling it an act of God...

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.290
...it should be called a trick by the Devil...

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.780
Du... el...?

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:33.000
Do not tell me you are not going to accept, Marquis.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:37.870
2nd Lieutenant...

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.890
This is good!

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:55.980
A duel!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.270
A duel, you say?

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.080
What are your conditions?

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.030
Arm wrestling?

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.570
Or possibly a game of tag?

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.080
A duel with swords.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.920
Don't tell me... she...

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.280
Gosh, I knew it!

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.570
Yo, big guy over there.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:38.690
A wall, please.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.960
This was the only thing she wouldn't give in to.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:04.280
It is the Emperor's Seal, after all.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.970
One <i>is  supposed to have it by their side at all times.</i>

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:43.440
She's wonderful.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:47.760
The 2nd Lieutenant's always so...

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.510
so...

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:57.390
Sisters.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:04.480
I may not be able to protect your lives.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.740
Sorry for having you wait, Marquis.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.020
Very well.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:26.860
Then...

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.340
These two men are my swords.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.600
Come on, what's the matter?

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.220
Two against one?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:53.710
H...uh?

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.530
2nd Lieutenant?

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.040
Quit joking!

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:04.560
What I desired,

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:05.750
Marquis Paul,

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.500
was three against one, including you!

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:23.940
En garde!

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:29.730
Tell me!

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.900
If something like this had happened to her, what would the 2nd Lieutenant have done?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.570
What would she-

00:08:35.270 --> 00:08:36.280
What would she have-

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.120
2nd Lieutenant this, 2nd Lieutenant that...

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.920
You plan on being like that for the rest of your life?!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.320
The LT's not always the absolute answer, either.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:55.210
But I just don't know!

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.140
What should I have done...

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:01.030
How should I have...

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.150
If you're going to associate yourself with Section III,

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:15.330
then shouldn't you figure out that answer by yourself?

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:24.330
No!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.580
Corporal...

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.100
No, Lieutenant!

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:44.930
What do you mean, no?

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.020
You stay out of this.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.690
I'm not going to let you fight anymore.

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:55.690
2nd Lieutenant?!

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.050
What are you say-

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.910
Back off, Corporal!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:13.330
A flail... eh?

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.970
How pointless.

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:21.250
Let's go three versus two.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.400
So I was right.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:33.400
I was wondering about you two.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.440
Round glasses made of brass...

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.400
You two...

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:39.770
...are Royal Guards from Loderia.

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:43.570
Loderia, as in... that?

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:45.270
Ahh...

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.620
The history of the agricultural country of Loderia...

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.750
...is a history filled with civil farmer riots.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:53.220
I heard that by using their knowledge in quelling the riots,

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:58.230
they have created a guild of professional mercenaries hired solely to protect VIPs.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:06.720
For being professionals at quelling farmer riots,

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.230
they really don't care about
the actual situation right now, eh?

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.370
Come on, come on, come on, what's the matter?

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:18.570
This is not good.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:22.990
We might not be able to do anything this time.

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:36.290
If... If I get hit by this...

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.890
Don't stop, Corporal!

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:56.510
You have a voice that fits very well for a commander.

00:11:56.990 --> 00:12:02.090
If not for you, that soldier's head would be split wide open now.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.260
Are you not going to go after him?

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:18.680
That won't be necessary.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:19.980
Right now,

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:24.550
I have not drawn my sword as a soldier or as his superior.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.700
I am from the Thirteen Appointed Families,

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.040
the third princess of the Malvin family,

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:37.100
Alice L. Malvin.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.750
A noble's sword exists to protect the people...

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:43.490
...and to fight against foreign enemies.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:04.510
I see.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:09.800
As expected from a woman from
the household of our former king of Loderia...

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:16.190
...who received the nickname, "Noble Flamme".

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:18.410
A matchete...

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.690
Is that fluid some sort of poison?

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.430
It doesn't look like it...

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:28.950
Unfortunately, the nickname was only bestowed upon my grandfather.

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:31.910
For this third princess...

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.450
...is a bit barbaric to be called noble!

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.030
He's a professional.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.880
Pros wouldn't take part in unreasonable fights.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.930
I just need to point the gun towards him.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.430
If he's a pro...

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.900
...then he'd surrender...

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:04.470
I would like to confirm something first.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:10.480
Since this is a duel, even if you're a noble of the Thirteen Families, I can kill you, right?

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:11.450
Of course.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:15.370
Anything else?

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:19.470
And what are you betting on this duel?

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:27.540
A noble's...

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:31.640
All nobles'...

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:35.640
...pride.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.100
Quit screwing around!

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:42.700
Pride?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.110
Pride, you say?

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:47.930
Nobles don't have no shitty pride.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.110
Like hell you have any!

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.730
You think this little game where you bet something that doesn't exist...

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.120
...will satisfy our feelings?!

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.360
Yeah!

00:14:58.360 --> 00:14:59.670
You ain't foolin' us!

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.040
We're gonna butcher y'all!

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:18.270
Yo.

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:24.650
You call that hiding?!

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.410
I must've ripped your stomach apart.

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:46.610
Drop your weapon.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.260
With that sobbing face and blood you spit all over the place,

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.260
you're telling me to drop my weapon?

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.360
I'm not bluffing.

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:57.680
Drop your weapon.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.140
If you don't-

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.170
What do you think?

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.480
It's scary, isn't it?

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.520
You are my prey, after all.

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:08.880
Compared to this,

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:14.740
you and your gun are just huge, not scary at all.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.200
Having done all this,

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:20.560
we're going to get the death penalty anyway!

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:21.530
Yeah!

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:25.200
So the more we kill, the more we get out of this!

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:25.880
Right?

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:27.000
Yeah!

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:27.970
Let's do it!

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:29.050
Butcher 'em!

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.880
Can I have a moment?

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:34.880
Begging for your lives now won't-

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:41.390
You're-

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:08.080
You're a... noble, too?

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:12.070
The fact that documents like these exist...

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.940
...makes the Marquis' wrongdoings clear and evident.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.540
Then, if the princess were to win the duel,

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:24.440
the Marquis will be subpoenaed
to appear in court and admit his guilt.

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:31.230
And... all of you will be considered prosecutors of justice...

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.210
...and will be released without any charges.

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:35.190
Without any charges?

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:37.040
He's lying, isn't he?

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:39.450
And if we win?

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:43.160
Whatever the Marquis wishes to do.

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:46.520
He may deny his wrongdoing and keep it a secret,

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:49.980
or he may plan about how to escape this place.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:53.220
Well, but then,

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:59.050
a massacre of us all will simply continue as scheduled.

00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:03.220
What say you?

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.380
Wh-Why not?

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:11.110
Yeah, no matter who wins, we don't lose.

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:14.040
So if the third princess wins...

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:16.570
Yeah... there will be no massacre...

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:20.010
We'll be saved, right?

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.410
We'll be saved!

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:26.880
Is it really okay...

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.370
...to trust that man like this?

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:31.880
Hey, what'll we do?

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.610
We'll let you do your duel, that's all.

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:39.470
We won't back away from anything else.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:43.840
Well, my Princess,

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:45.200
fight as much as you please-

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:45.770
Do not come near me!

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:50.210
We're in the middle of a duel with the pride of nobles on the line!

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:52.640
She...

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.150
He's good...

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.670
Leonir Taylor...

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:02.450
With his tongue, this whole assault might not have even taken place.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.190
Indeed.

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:08.990
Most of the nobles here are second or third-grade families.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:12.120
In fact, most of them are second-born sons and daughters.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.790
People like them don't care about their honor,

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.310
will scrape at any chance to protect their lives,

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:22.720
and do all they can to make the commoners heroes and Paul the villain.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:24.430
But...

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:27.730
That guy doesn't get it at all.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:32.940
The reason why these people raised forks and hoes and charged into this place...

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:35.940
He doesn't understand the real reason.

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:41.450
Reasons of justice or awards won't make these commoners lay down their weapons.

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:44.450
It's not that they can't tolerate evil.

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.240
It's not that they can't tolerate poverty.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.890
They could have survived if they did wrong, too.

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:53.310
They could have survived if nobles were poor, too.

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:59.760
What they can't tolerate... is this entire world of unfairness.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:03.760
Something like that can't be solved by a duel!

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:05.770
No...

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.770
This won't stop it...

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:09.330
This mustn't stop us!

00:20:11.300 --> 00:20:13.100
Hey, big guy.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.740
Did you know?

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:20.020
No matter how much you point a gun at normal people,

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:22.490
they just don't really get scared.

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.660
Well, there's no helping that.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.490
It's hard to imagine the pain of getting shot by a gun.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.410
Other than soldiers or criminal suspects,

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:34.070
there's really not that many people that have been shot.

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:38.500
So civilian mobs are ill-natured.

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.550
A gun and a knife.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:49.560
They probably are more scared of a knife touching their skin than a gun, right?

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:52.870
In mob fights,

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:58.680
you keep the opposition in check by making them know what kind of pain will come to them.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:02.690
Cutting...

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:03.770
Hitting...

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:05.130
Smashing...

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:09.580
The more primitive the pain, the more effective!

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.910
In painful forms...

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.960
With painful sounds...

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:20.870
Butcher a few of them into mincemeat...

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:24.220
...and the pussy ones can't do anything anymore!

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.220
Never stop the engine, okay?

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:30.720
These guys could go on a rampage any moment now.

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:37.230
I would like to add another condition for our victory.

00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:42.440
If I win, I get that car as a means of escape; is that okay?

00:21:43.250 --> 00:21:44.450
Very well.

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:45.440
Do what you want.

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:47.990
Then, we accept...

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:49.620
...this duel!!

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:36.270
Mer-kun, having accepted the feelings of both the nobles and the commoners, Alice's duel continues.

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:38.830
And Mr. Fiancé is just standing there and watching?

00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:41.080
Next time, "The Solitary Balance."

00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:43.080
Come get us if you dare!
